
kgf 0.6
language: reltext

=== features
# A toy spec: a format-specific experiment, selected explicitly
# (`--spec=reltext`) rather than by extension. It never claimed one — its
# `.rel` fixtures are passed by name — and `detection_scope: overlay` says so
# in the same terms as its siblings, which had to give theirs up because
# several of them claimed the same `.b64`, `.hex` and `.txt`.
detection_scope: overlay

=== lex
SKIP        /(\s+)+/
TOKEN ARROW     /->/
TOKEN COLON     /:/
TOKEN Ident     /[^\s:]+/

=== grammar
Doc        -> ( Line )*
Line       -> from:Ident ARROW to:Ident (COLON kind:Ident)?

=== attrs
on Line:    import module=to ; import module=from

=== semantics
on Line {
  edge moduleDependsOn from $file to $resolve($to) attrs obj("via", $to, "dep_kind", "value")
  edge moduleDependsOn from $file to $resolve($from) attrs obj("via", $from, "dep_kind", "value")
}

=== resolver
relative_prefixes: ./, ../, /, http://, https://, url:, npm:, pip:
exts:
indexes:
bare_prefix:
module_path_style: slash
